# Vantage 33M ATC test config — machine I/O for the toolchanger (Beckhoff
# EK1100 + terminals, see ethercat-conf.xml). Commented out: the EK1100
# coupler isn't on the test bench yet. Uncomment here and in
# ethercat-conf.xml together once it is — don't enable only one file, or
# slave indices/pin names will mismatch.
#
# The M6/M106 remaps (remap/) drive the toolchanger purely through the core
# `motion` component's motion.digital-out-NN / motion.probe-input pins (see
# num_dio=16 in ethercat.hal), so those nets are what needs wiring to real
# Beckhoff channels below — the remap .ngc files never reference lcec pins
# directly.
#
# Channel assignments:
#   digital-out-00..06 -> vertical drills V1..V7   (T101-T107)
#   digital-out-07..10 -> horizontal drills, in order X+, X-, Y+, Y- (T201-T204)
#   digital-out-11     -> spindle drawbar unclamp solenoid (energized = unclamp/release,
#                         de-energized = spring-clamped/grip — verify this against
#                         the actual spindle/valve before running; if reversed,
#                         swap the M64/M65 senses in remap/return_tool.ngc and
#                         remap/fetch_tool.ngc rather than here)
#   digital-out-12     -> Marposs touch probe deploy/retract solenoid (energized = deployed,
#                         de-energized = retracted — same "verify before running" caveat as
#                         above; if reversed, swap the M64/M65 senses in remap/m107_remap.ngc
#                         and remap/m108_remap.ngc rather than here)
#   digital-out-13..15 -> spare
#   probe-input        -> OR of two physical probes — LinuxCNC only has one probe input, and
#                         these two are never both in position to trip at once in correctly
#                         sequenced g-code:
#                           - tool height probe (fixed location, see remap/atc-positions.ngc)
#                           - Marposs touch probe (workpiece probing; mounted on a pneumatic
#                             actuator next to the HSK63F spindle, not in a tool holder — see
#                             remap/m107_remap.ngc, remap/m108_remap.ngc, and README.md
#                             "Workpiece Touch Probe (Marposs)")

# --- EL2808 #1 (digital outputs, slave idx 6) — vertical drills ---
# net atc-vdrill-1-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-0   <= motion.digital-out-00
# net atc-vdrill-2-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-1   <= motion.digital-out-01
# net atc-vdrill-3-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-2   <= motion.digital-out-02
# net atc-vdrill-4-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-3   <= motion.digital-out-03
# net atc-vdrill-5-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-4   <= motion.digital-out-04
# net atc-vdrill-6-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-5   <= motion.digital-out-05
# net atc-vdrill-7-out => lcec.0.io-dout1.dout-6   <= motion.digital-out-06
# # dout-7 spare

# --- EL2808 #2 (digital outputs, slave idx 8) — horizontal drills + drawbar ---
# net atc-hdrill-xplus-out  => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-0 <= motion.digital-out-07
# net atc-hdrill-xminus-out => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-1 <= motion.digital-out-08
# net atc-hdrill-yplus-out  => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-2 <= motion.digital-out-09
# net atc-hdrill-yminus-out => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-3 <= motion.digital-out-10
# net atc-drawbar-unclamp   => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-4 <= motion.digital-out-11
# net marposs-probe-deploy  => lcec.0.io-dout2.dout-5 <= motion.digital-out-12
# # dout-6..7 spare

# --- EL1808 #1 (digital inputs, slave idx 5) — tool height probe + Marposs touch probe ---
# Both physical probes feed the single motion.probe-input pin through an or2,
# since G38.x and the M106 remap only ever look at one probe input. Safe
# because a correctly sequenced program never has both probes in position to
# trip at the same time (see channel assignments above).
# loadrt or2 names=probe-in-or
# addf probe-in-or servo-thread
# net atc-probe-in      <= lcec.0.io-din1.din-0 => probe-in-or.in0
# net marposs-probe-in  <= lcec.0.io-din1.din-1 => probe-in-or.in1
# net probe-in-combined <= probe-in-or.out      => motion.probe-input
# # din-2..7 spare / TODO: assign (pocket-occupied sensors, drawbar-confirm, etc.)
